      "text": "# Serving Performance Experiment: Global Expert Pool with Concurrent Long Requests\n\n## 1. Experiment Overview\n\n### Objective\nMeasure the end-to-end serving performance of the Global Expert Pool implementation under concurrent long-sequence decode workloads, focusing on:\n- **Throughput**: tokens/second across concurrent requests\n- **Latency**: per-token decode latency distribution\n- **Cache efficiency**: hit/miss rates, promotion/staging behavior\n- **Memory pressure**: pool utilization, eviction frequency, staging row contention\n- **Scalability**: performance degradation as concurrency increases\n\n### Workload Design: Four Concurrent Long Requests\nFour independent decode streams, each generating a long sequence (e.g., 2048\u20134096 tokens), simulating realistic serving scenarios where multiple users share the same MoE model with a constrained VRAM expert pool.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Measurement Plan\n\n### 2.1 Configuration Parameters\n\n| Parameter | Value | Rationale |\n|-----------|-------|-----------|\n| `num_layers` | 32 | Typical MoE transformer depth |\n| `num_experts` | 128 | Per-layer expert count |\n| `slots_per_layer` | `[16, 16, 16, 16, ...]` (32 entries) | 16 resident experts per layer \u2192 512 pool rows total |\n| `staging` | 16 | Shared staging rows for overflow misses |\n| `PLAN_WIDTH` | 16 | Max experts selected per token per layer |\n| `gate` | 1 (open) | Enable promotions |\n| `promote_limit` | 4 | Max promotions per layer call |\n| `promote_interval` | 1 | Promote every forward |\n| `promote_min_misses` | 2 | Require 2 misses before promotion |\n| `protect_recent` | 2 | Protect rows used in last 2 forwards |\n| `batch_size` | 4 | Four concurrent requests |\n| `seq_length` | 2048 | Long sequence decode |\n| `top_k` | 8 | Experts selected per token per layer |\n| `device` | CUDA | GPU execution |\n\n### 2.2 Metrics Collected\n\n#### Per-Step Metrics (from `StepBuffers`)\n- `gather_count`: total experts fetched (promotions + staged)\n- `",
