      "text": "# Debugging Guide: Long-Context Concurrent Inference with EXL3 GPU Expert Cache\n\n## Overview\n\nThis guide addresses debugging challenges specific to **long-context concurrent inference** using the EXL3 GPU expert cache system. The documentation explicitly states that *\"Long-context behavior and broader model quality remain unqualified\"* and that *\"Full 131K input and 32K output remain untested.\"* This means you are operating in uncharted territory where standard debugging approaches may fail.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Understanding the Constraints\n\n### Key Limitations from Documentation\n\n| Constraint | Value | Implication |\n|------------|-------|-------------|\n| Max decode routing lanes | 64 | `sequences \u00d7 (1 + draft_tokens) \u00d7 top_k \u2264 64` |\n| Default context | 2,048 tokens | Long context requires explicit configuration |\n| KV cache (no MTP) | 4 GiB | May be insufficient for 131K context |\n| KV cache (with MTP) | 4.5 GiB | Tested at 131K, but not validated for concurrency |\n| Concurrent sequences | 1 (tested) | Multi-sequence behavior is unqualified |\n| Prefill mode | Eager-only | No CUDA graph support for prefill |\n\n### Critical Formula for Lane Budget\n\n```python\ndef check_lane_budget(num_sequences: int, num_draft_tokens: int, top_k: int = 10) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    The routing planner supports at most 64 lanes.\n    sequences \u00d7 (1 + draft_tokens) \u00d7 top_k must fit that bound.\n    \"\"\"\n    lanes = num_sequences * (1 + num_draft_tokens) * top_k\n    return lanes <= 64\n\n# Example: 4 sequences with MTP3 (3 draft tokens)\n# 4 \u00d7 (1 + 3) \u00d7 10 = 160 lanes \u2192 EXCEEDS 64 limit!\nprint(check_lane_budget(4, 3))  # False\n\n# Example: 1 sequence with MTP3\n# 1 \u00d7 (1 + 3) \u00d7 10 = 40 lanes \u2192 Within limit\nprint(check_lane_budget(1, 3))  # True\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Memory Budgeting for Long Context\n\n### Calculating KV Cache Requirements\n\nFor long-context inference, KV",
